## Landed (2026-11-21)

In main since round 168 (ee391287b7, `LANDING/2026-11-21T2340Z-KRN-landed-ee391287.md` on `internal-dev-messages`), with DRV's 213-DRV-0085, 0086 (`display` replaces the stub and keeps its lines) and 0087. The gate passed every group on both architectures: every PCI grant of every QEMU boot went through the changed transition. Round 167 was not landed, because APP's request failed the network group and was returned.

**Left:** the Ryzen's run (DRV), with the lines the acceptance criteria name. A stick written from main carries it.

## Resolution

Made in `kernel/src/pci_control.rs` (`Mode::Memory`), `kernel/src/pci.rs`, `kernel/src/scheduler.rs` (`MEM_MAP` write-combining in the boot framebuffer's BAR) and `init` (the windows, `PLATFORM_ACPI_TABLE`'s VFCT copy). Landed in round 168.

**On the Ryzen:** DRV's run 0 (2026-11-21 18:26 UTC, release 202611211819; recorded in [213-DRV-0086](../issues/213-DRV-0086-display-the-second-output-lit.md), section "Run 0 on the Ryzen"). Its tree was DRV's bench build on round 167's candidate (5667eb9655), which carried this grant at 809d741c74. `kernel/src/pci.rs`, `kernel/src/pci_control.rs`, `kernel/src/scheduler.rs`, `init/src/main.rs` and `init/src/hardware.rs` are the same there as on `main` since round 168. Its lines:
- `init`: `COMMAND 0006 BEFORE THE GRANT, 0006 AFTER; BAR 5 0x0+0x1B000 AND 0x58000+0x1000` and `VBIOS: THE VFCT TABLE, 55428 BYTES, READ-ONLY`;
- `display`: `BAR 5 AT FCB00000: 108 KIB OF ITS REGISTERS GRANTED`, `THE SMU MAILBOX: 4096 BYTES GRANTED`, `BAR 0 FOR A SECOND SCREEN: 20480 KIB GRANTED`, `VBIOS: VFCT 55428 BYTES, AN IMAGE FOR 1002:1638 OF 55296 BYTES, ROM SIGNATURE 55AA` (the image is the 55,296 bytes Linux read);
- `COMMAND 0006 AFTER STEP 1`.

**First light** on HDMI-A-1 went through this grant on 2026-11-22 at 04:43 UTC (release 202611220438, DRV's report `KRN/2026-11-22T0448Z-DRV-first-light-on-the-ryzens-second-output-through-your-grant.md` on `internal-dev-messages`):
- the engine's window [0, 0x1B000) held the eight batches, the eight stages and tables 12, 4 and 76 as the hardware ran them;
- the command register stayed 0006;
- `display` asked for nothing beyond the mailbox page and the VBIOS copy;
- the maintainer saw HDMI-A-1 show the engine's colour squares and DP-2 show MIND Core's screen. Nobody watched DP-2 while the stages ran, so whether it flickered is not known.

The carve-out question in "Not covered" is answered by DRV's run 7 in 213-DRV-0086. The firmware's map marks 0x8_0E30_0000 to 0x8_2FFF_FFFF as reserved, and the frame pool takes only conventional memory, so the frame pool never hands out the carve-out.

The compositor's part is [213-KRN-0272](213-KRN-0272-a-second-screen-for-the-compositor.done).

This is evidence for that machine with those builds (MC-12.1).

